IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa-definitions-tests.l4: tests of coa-core.l4 and coa-definitions.l4.
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the provision (the text of ukpga-2006-46.txt, a plain-text rendering,
-- not the official text) BEFORE the assertion was run, and is written beside the assertion. A failing assertion is a
-- finding; no expected value was edited to match the code. Each #ASSERT is on one line.
-- Positional arguments follow the GIVEN order of the function under test, set out in coa-definitions.l4.
--
-- Reading an answer: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text
-- does not decide). T and F below are TRUE and FALSE.

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
T MEANS TRUE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
F MEANS FALSE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- THE CORE IS USABLE: its nouns can be built, compared and used in a deontic on the stable binary
-- =========================================================================================================

`fixture: the director declares the interest` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "declare the nature and extent of the interest"

-- s 182: a director must declare the nature and extent of the interest (the section is another part's; this only
-- proves the generic action works in a DEONTIC on the stable binary).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`fixture: duty to declare` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `fixture: the director declares the interest`
    WITHIN 28

#TRACE `fixture: duty to declare` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `fixture: the director declares the interest` AT 10

-- s 84(1)(b): "a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default
-- fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale" on summary conviction, no imprisonment.
`fixture: the s 84(1)(b) penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `fixture: the s 84(1)(b) penalty`'s `how convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `fixture: the s 84(1)(b) penalty`'s `imprisonment not exceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `fixture: the s 84(1)(b) penalty`'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
#ASSERT `fixture: the s 84(1)(b) penalty`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)

-- s 183(2)(a): "on conviction on indictment, to a fine" (no stated limit).
`fixture: the s 183(2)(a) penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `fixture: the s 183(2)(a) penalty`'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`

-- A Period of 28 days, and the individual in the seat identified by a reference field.
`fixture: 28 days` MEANS Period WITH `number of units` IS 28, unit IS Days
#ASSERT `fixture: 28 days`'s unit EQUALS Days
#ASSERT `fixture: 28 days`'s `number of units` EQUALS 28
`fixture: an individual born 1 February 1990` MEANS Individual WITH `reference for the individual` IS "ind-1", `date of birth` IS Date 1 2 1990
#ASSERT `fixture: an individual born 1 February 1990`'s `date of birth` EQUALS Date 1 2 1990
-- Line 4 of the text gives the date of enactment, [8th November 2006].
#ASSERT `the Companies Act 2006 was enacted on` EQUALS Date 8 11 2006

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 1
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 1(1) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Arguments: formed after commencement (a); formed under 1985 Act/1986 Order immediately before (b)(i);
-- existing company (b)(ii); the context otherwise requires.
-- (a) alone: a company.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the body is a company` T F F F EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(i) alone: a company.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the body is a company` F T F F EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(ii) alone: a company.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the body is a company` F F T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of (a), (b)(i), (b)(ii): "means" is closed, so no.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the body is a company` F F F F EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless the context otherwise requires": the definition is switched off, so the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the body is a company` T F F T EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the body is a company` F F F T EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1(2) and (3): signposts, answered JUST TRUE where they apply and NOTHING elsewhere -----------------
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(a) Chapter 1 of Part 33 applies to the company` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(a) Chapter 1 of Part 33 applies to the company` F EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(b) Chapter 2 of Part 33 applies to the body` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(b) Chapter 2 of Part 33 applies to the body` F EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(3) Part 34 is where the Companies Acts deal with the company` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(3) Part 34 is where the Companies Acts deal with the company` F EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 2 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVEN e IS A `s 2 enactment`
      p IS A `s 2 place in the enactment`
      inForce IS A BOOLEAN
      applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2 provision`
`fixture: provision of` MEANS `s 2 provision` WITH
    `s 2 enactment of the provision` IS e
    `s 2 place of the provision` IS p
    `remaining in force` IS inForce
    `applying for the purposes of Parts 1 to 39` IS applies

-- Arguments of `fixture: provision of`: enactment, place, remaining in force, applying for the purposes of Parts 1 to 39.
-- s 2(2)(a): Parts 1 to 39 of this Act are company law provisions. Boundaries 1, 39 and 40.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 1) T F) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 39) T F) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Parts 40 to 44 are in neither list: the definition is a closed list (fork F1 in NOTES.md), so no.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 40) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 44) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2(2)(b): Parts 45 to 47 "so far as they apply for the purposes of those Parts". Boundaries 45 and 47.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 45) T T) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 45) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 47) T T) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 47) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A Schedule is not named in s 2(2): silent.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` `s 2 in a Schedule` T F) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(2) speaks of "this Act" only.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 1985` (`s 2 in a Part` 1) T F) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 2(1)(a): through s 2(2).
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 10) T F) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` (`s 2 in a Part` 42) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2(1)(b): Part 2 of the 2004 Act only.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` (`s 2 in a Part` 2) T F) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` (`s 2 in a Part` 1) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` (`s 2 in a Part` 3) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` `s 2 in a Schedule` T F) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(1)(c): provisions of the 1985 Acts "that remain in force".
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 1985` (`s 2 in a Part` 5) T F) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Act 1985` (`s 2 in a Part` 5) F F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985` (`s 2 in a Part` 1) T F) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985` (`s 2 in a Part` 1) F F) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Any other enactment: "means" is closed.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` (`fixture: provision of` `s 2 another enactment` (`s 2 in a Part` 1) T F) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 3 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rows: no limit; shares; guarantee; some other limit. Columns: (1) limited, (2) by shares, (3) by guarantee, (4) unlimited.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the company is limited by guarantee` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the company is limited by guarantee` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the company is limited by guarantee` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Limited "by its constitution" in a way neither (2) nor (3) names: limited under (1); neither of (2), (3), (4).
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the company is limited by guarantee` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 4 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 4(3): "Great Britain" 22 December 1980; Northern Ireland 1 July 1983.
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the relevant date` `England and Wales` EQUALS Date 22 12 1980
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the relevant date` `Scotland` EQUALS Date 22 12 1980
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the relevant date` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS Date 1 7 1983
#ASSERT NOT ((`s 4(3) the relevant date` `Northern Ireland`) EQUALS (`s 4(3) the relevant date` `Scotland`))

-- Arguments of `fixture: profile of`: place, liability, a share capital, certificate states public.
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
      shareCapital IS A BOOLEAN
      certificate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Company profile`
`fixture: profile of` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS place
    `liability of the members` IS liability
    `a share capital` IS shareCapital
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS certificate

`fixture: a public company limited by shares` MEANS `fixture: profile of` `England and Wales` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` T T
`fixture: a public company limited by guarantee` MEANS `fixture: profile of` `Scotland` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` T T
`fixture: a private company limited by shares` MEANS `fixture: profile of` `England and Wales` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` T F
`fixture: a company limited by shares without a share capital` MEANS `fixture: profile of` `England and Wales` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` F T
`fixture: an unlimited company whose certificate says public` MEANS `fixture: profile of` `England and Wales` `liability not limited` T T
`fixture: a company otherwise limited whose certificate says public` MEANS `fixture: profile of` `Northern Ireland` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` T T

-- s 4(2): the last argument is "requirements ... complied with on or after the relevant date".
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: a public company limited by shares` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: a public company limited by guarantee` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) not complied with: no.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: a public company limited by shares` F EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) the certificate does not say it is public: no.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: a private company limited by shares` T EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no share capital: no.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: a company limited by shares without a share capital` T EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- unlimited, or limited in some other way: not "limited by shares or limited by guarantee".
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: an unlimited company whose certificate says public` T EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `fixture: a company otherwise limited whose certificate says public` T EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 4(1): a private company is any company that is not a public company.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `fixture: a public company limited by shares` T EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `fixture: a public company limited by shares` F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `fixture: a private company limited by shares` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `fixture: an unlimited company whose certificate says public` T EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 5 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5(1): arguments: would be limited by guarantee, would have a share capital.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) a company can be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` T T EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) a company can be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` T F EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1) a company can be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` F T EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1) a company can be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` F F EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(2): in force in Great Britain since 22 December 1980; in Northern Ireland since 1 July 1983.
#ASSERT `s 5(2) the date from which s 5(1) has been in force` `England and Wales` EQUALS Date 22 12 1980
#ASSERT `s 5(2) the date from which s 5(1) has been in force` `Scotland` EQUALS Date 22 12 1980
#ASSERT `s 5(2) the date from which s 5(1) has been in force` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS Date 1 7 1983
-- s 5(3): arguments: limited by guarantee, purports to divide into shares or interests, nominal value or number specified.
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the constitutional provision is a provision for a share capital` T T T EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "whether or not the nominal value or number of the shares or interests is specified".
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the constitutional provision is a provision for a share capital` T T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the constitutional provision is a provision for a share capital` F T T EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the constitutional provision is a provision for a share capital` T F T EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 6 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Arguments: liability, a share capital, way (formed as one, or becoming one).
-- (a) a company limited by shares: formed or becoming.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` T `s 6(1) being formed as one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` T `s 6(1) becoming one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) a company limited by guarantee and not having a share capital: formed or becoming.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` F `s 6(1) being formed as one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` F `s 6(1) becoming one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital: may become.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` T `s 6(1) becoming one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) says only "become": formed as one is not said.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` T `s 6(1) being formed as one` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An unlimited company, or one limited in another way: not named; the 2004 Act is outside the sources.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability not limited` F `s 6(1) becoming one` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` F `s 6(1) becoming one` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(2).
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the provision has effect subject to Part 2 of the 2004 Act` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the provision has effect subject to Part 2 of the 2004 Act` F EQUALS NOTHING

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 38
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 1158 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Arguments: registered under this Act; an overseas company that has registered particulars under s 1046.
#ASSERT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` F F EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "The expression does not include an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046."
#ASSERT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` T T EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` F T EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1159 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A link, positionally: (a) holds a majority of the voting rights; (b) member with the right to appoint or remove a
-- majority of the board; (c) member controlling alone, under an agreement with other members, a majority of the votes.
`fixture: a link with a majority of the votes` MEANS `s 1159(1) link` OF T, F, F
`fixture: a link with the board right` MEANS `s 1159(1) link` OF F, T, F
`fixture: a link controlling alone by agreement` MEANS `s 1159(1) link` OF F, F, T
`fixture: a link meeting none of (a) to (c)` MEANS `s 1159(1) link` OF F, F, F

#ASSERT `s 1159(1)(a)-(c) the other company is directly the holding company of the company` `fixture: a link with a majority of the votes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1)(a)-(c) the other company is directly the holding company of the company` `fixture: a link with the board right` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1)(a)-(c) the other company is directly the holding company of the company` `fixture: a link controlling alone by agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1)(a)-(c) the other company is directly the holding company of the company` `fixture: a link meeting none of (a) to (c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Routes: one route with one link is the direct case; a route with two links is "a subsidiary of a company that is
-- itself a subsidiary of that other company".
`fixture: a route of one link meeting (a)` MEANS `s 1159(1) route` OF LIST `fixture: a link with a majority of the votes`
`fixture: a route of one link meeting none` MEANS `s 1159(1) route` OF LIST `fixture: a link meeting none of (a) to (c)`
`fixture: a route of two links each meeting a limb` MEANS `s 1159(1) route` OF LIST `fixture: a link with a majority of the votes`, `fixture: a link with the board right`
`fixture: a route whose second link meets none` MEANS `s 1159(1) route` OF LIST `fixture: a link with a majority of the votes`, `fixture: a link meeting none of (a) to (c)`
`fixture: a route with no links` MEANS `s 1159(1) route` OF EMPTY

#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `fixture: a route of one link meeting (a)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `fixture: a route of two links each meeting a limb`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `fixture: a route of one link meeting none`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `fixture: a route whose second link meets none`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `fixture: a route with no links`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Two routes: it is enough that one holds.
#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `fixture: a route of one link meeting none`, `fixture: a route of one link meeting (a)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No relation stated at all: the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1159(2): "no members except that other and that other's wholly-owned subsidiaries or persons acting on behalf of
-- that other or its wholly-owned subsidiaries".
#ASSERT `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `s 1159(2) the other company itself`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `s 1159(2) the other company itself`, `s 1159(2) a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company`, `s 1159(2) a person acting on behalf of the other company`, `s 1159(2) a person acting on behalf of a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `s 1159(2) the other company itself`, `s 1159(2) anyone else`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` (LIST `s 1159(2) anyone else`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1159(4): "company" includes any body corporate.
#ASSERT `s 1159(4) the body is a company for the purposes of s 1159 and Schedule 6` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1159(4) the body is a company for the purposes of s 1159 and Schedule 6` F EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1161 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1161(1): arguments: the kind of entity, whether an association carries on a trade or business.
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `a partnership` F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `an unincorporated association` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `an unincorporated association` F EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A corporation sole is not a "body corporate" (s 1173(1)(a)) and is neither a partnership nor an association.
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `a corporation sole` T EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` `an individual` T EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 1161(2)(a): arguments: the undertaking has capital but no share capital; the right is a right to share in the capital.
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(a) the right is a share in the undertaking` T T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(a) the right is a share in the undertaking` T F EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(a) the right is a share in the undertaking` F T EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1161(2)(b): arguments: without capital; (i) a right to share in profits or a liability for losses; (ii) an obligation to contribute to debts or expenses on a winding up.
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(b) the interest is a share in the undertaking` T T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(b) the interest is a share in the undertaking` T F T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(b) the interest is a share in the undertaking` T F F EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1161(2)(b) the interest is a share in the undertaking` F T T EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1161(3): arguments: the undertaking is not a company; a specific context provides for the translation.
#ASSERT `s 1161(3) the expression appropriate to companies is construed as a reference to the corresponding person, officer, document or organ of the undertaking` T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(3) the expression appropriate to companies is construed as a reference to the corresponding person, officer, document or organ of the undertaking` T T EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1161(3) the expression appropriate to companies is construed as a reference to the corresponding person, officer, document or organ of the undertaking` F F EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1161(4): arguments: both are subsidiary undertakings of the same parent undertaking; either is a parent or subsidiary undertaking of the other.
#ASSERT `s 1161(4) the two undertakings are fellow subsidiary undertakings` T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(4) the two undertakings are fellow subsidiary undertakings` T T EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1161(4) the two undertakings are fellow subsidiary undertakings` F F EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1161(5): arguments: a parent or subsidiary undertaking of that undertaking; a subsidiary undertaking of any parent undertaking of it.
#ASSERT `s 1161(5) the undertaking is a group undertaking in relation to the other undertaking` T F EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(5) the undertaking is a group undertaking in relation to the other undertaking` F T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1161(5) the undertaking is a group undertaking in relation to the other undertaking` F F EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1162 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A relation, positionally (the order of the DECLARE):
--   holds a majority of the voting rights | member | right to appoint or remove a majority of the board |
--   dominant influence by the articles | dominant influence by a control contract | controls alone a majority by agreement |
--   a subsidiary undertaking of it is a member | shares held by a person acting on behalf of it or its subsidiaries |
--   has the power to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control | managed on a unified basis |
--   a subsidiary undertaking of it is, or is to be treated as, a parent undertaking of that undertaking
`fixture: holds a majority of the voting rights` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF T, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: a member with the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, T, T, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: the board right without membership` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, T, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: the board right and a subsidiary undertaking is a member` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, T, F, F, F, T, F, F, F, F
`fixture: the board right and shares are held by a nominee` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, T, F, F, F, F, T, F, F, F
`fixture: a dominant influence by the articles` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, T, F, F, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: a dominant influence by a control contract` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, F, T, F, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: a member controlling alone by agreement` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, T, F, F, F, T, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: controlling alone by agreement without membership` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, F, F, T, F, F, F, F, F
`fixture: unified management` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, T, F
`fixture: the power to exercise dominant influence` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, T, F, F
`fixture: a subsidiary undertaking is a parent undertaking` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, T
`fixture: no limb of s 1162` MEANS `s 1162 relation` OF F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F, F

-- s 1162(2): (a) a majority of the voting rights; (b) a member with the board right; (c)(i) articles, (c)(ii) control contract;
-- (d) a member controlling alone by agreement. "Member" includes "treated as a member" by s 1162(3).
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: holds a majority of the voting rights` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: a member with the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: the board right without membership` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: the board right and a subsidiary undertaking is a member` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: the board right and shares are held by a nominee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: a dominant influence by the articles` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: a dominant influence by a control contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: a member controlling alone by agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: controlling alone by agreement without membership` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: no limb of s 1162` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Subsection (4) says "also": unified management alone is not a limb of (2).
#ASSERT `s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: unified management` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1162(3): treated as a member.
#ASSERT `s 1162(3) the undertaking is treated as a member of the other undertaking` `fixture: a member with the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(3) the undertaking is treated as a member of the other undertaking` `fixture: the board right and a subsidiary undertaking is a member` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(3) the undertaking is treated as a member of the other undertaking` `fixture: the board right and shares are held by a nominee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(3) the undertaking is treated as a member of the other undertaking` `fixture: the board right without membership` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1162(4): (a) the power to exercise, or actually exercising, dominant influence or control; (b) managed on a unified basis.
#ASSERT `s 1162(4) the first undertaking is also a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: unified management` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(4) the first undertaking is also a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: the power to exercise dominant influence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(4) the first undertaking is also a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: no limb of s 1162` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1162(4) the first undertaking is also a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: holds a majority of the voting rights` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1162(5): treated as the parent undertaking of undertakings of which a subsidiary undertaking is (or is treated as) a parent.
#ASSERT `s 1162(5) the first undertaking is treated as a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: a subsidiary undertaking is a parent undertaking` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(5) the first undertaking is treated as a parent undertaking of the second` `fixture: no limb of s 1162` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1162(7): references to shares are to allotted shares.
#ASSERT `s 1162(7) the reference to shares is a reference to the shares` T EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1162(7) the reference to shares is a reference to the shares` F EQUALS JUST FALSE

