-- The borrowed terms: JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE pass through; NOTHING means the borrowed definition is not known.
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) credit institution` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) the data protection legislation` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) EU regulated market` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) financial institution` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) hire-purchase agreement` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) regulated activity` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) regulated market` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) transferable securities` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) UK regulated market` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) credit institution` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) credit institution` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` `s 1173(1) UK regulated market` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "firm": any entity that is not an individual.
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `an individual` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `a corporation sole` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `a partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `an unincorporated association` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "the Gazette": London for England and Wales, Edinburgh for Scotland, Belfast for Northern Ireland.
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the Gazette for a company registered in the place` `England and Wales` EQUALS `s 1173(1) the London Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the Gazette for a company registered in the place` `Scotland` EQUALS `s 1173(1) the Edinburgh Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the Gazette for a company registered in the place` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS `s 1173(1) the Belfast Gazette`
-- "officer" includes a director, manager or secretary.
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1173(1) director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1173(1) manager` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1173(1) secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1173(1) another position` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "parent company": arguments: the person is a company; the s 1162 and Schedule 7 answer.
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` T (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` T (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` T NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` F (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "working day" for a company: not a Saturday or Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday, or a bank holiday in the part of the
-- United Kingdom where the company is registered. Dates worked out by hand: 1 January 2026 was a Thursday, so
-- Thursday 12 November 2026, Saturday 14 November 2026, Sunday 15 November 2026, Friday 25 December 2026 and Thursday
-- 24 December 2026; Friday 3 April 2026 was Good Friday; Friday 2 January 2026 is a bank holiday in Scotland only.
-- Arguments: the day; where the company is registered; the day is Good Friday; bank holidays in England and Wales, in
-- Scotland and in Northern Ireland.
`fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` MEANS LIST (Date 1 1 2026)
`fixture: bank holidays in Scotland on 1 and 2 January 2026` MEANS LIST (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 2 1 2026)

#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 12 11 2026) `England and Wales` F EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 24 12 2026) `England and Wales` F EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 14 11 2026) `England and Wales` F EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 15 11 2026) `Scotland` F EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 25 12 2026) `England and Wales` F EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 3 4 2026) `England and Wales` T EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 3 4 2026) `England and Wales` F EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The bank holiday that counts is the one in the part where the company is registered.
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 2 1 2026) `Scotland` F `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays in Scotland on 1 and 2 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 2 1 2026) `England and Wales` F `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays in Scotland on 1 and 2 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 2 1 2026) `Northern Ireland` F `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays in Scotland on 1 and 2 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date 1 1 2026) `Northern Ireland` F `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays in Scotland on 1 and 2 January 2026` `fixture: bank holidays on 1 January 2026` EQUALS JUST FALSE
